        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/_platform_common.py in the diff: `paths = read_platform_config(root).get(\"paths\")` and `checks_path = paths.get(\"checks\")`, followed by `git show {commit}:{checks_path}`. A candidate can edit `[paths] checks` to point at another TOML file that already exists at main and carries a `[[generated_files]]` table. The declared-generated set is then taken from that file instead of the real check configuration. The impact is limited to files main already declares, and no new path can be",
                  "id": "checks-path-read-from-working-tree",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "`generated_files()` takes the declaration file location from the working-tree `.dev-platform.toml`, which is candidate-controlled. The content is read at the observed main commit, but the file name is not. The spec and design say the declaration is read only from observed main and never from the can"
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
              "report_sha256": "628ec06f68e55b9a29e239a2458737cd13fc05e1e434325817fc01873e9897c3"
            },
            "spec-fidelity": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/_platform_common.py: in `classify_task_base_currency`, `generated_files(root, main_sha)` is called only inside the `merged.returncode == 1` branch after `conflicted` is non-empty. The tests are named `test_malformed_declaration_at_main_fails_explicitly_for_a_conflict` and `test_missing_check_configuration_at_main_fails_explicitly_for_a_conflict`, so they cover only the conflict path. The spec text (\"a malformed declaration SHALL fail explicitly\") and the agent-workflow.md paragr",
                  "id": "declaration-validated-only-on-conflict",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The spec and docs say a malformed declaration, a missing `paths.checks`, or a missing file at main \"fails explicitly\". The implementation reads the declaration only when the trial merge exits 1 with named conflicts. On a clean merge it is never read or validated, so the gate passes despite a malform"
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "spec-fidelity",
              "report_sha256": "d878038df3ac634f1fc3670301b916cac7de3764e0820585d116b7997b2f26c6"
            }
          },
